---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CountyMunicipalityMap from '../../../../components/jurisdictions/CountyMunicipalityMap.astro';
import PublicRecords from '../../../../components/jurisdictions/PublicRecords.astro';
import { winnebagoMunicipalities, winnebagoMunicipalitySources } from '../../../../data/illinois/counties/winnebago';
import { winnebagoCountyRecords } from '../../../../data/illinois/counties/winnebago-records';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Winnebago County Surveillance | NoRec.US"
  description="County and municipal surveillance research for Winnebago County, Illinois, including public records, ALPR, drones, and city-level dossiers."
  active="surveillance"
>
<main class="page_shell">
  <nav class="jurisdiction_breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/illinois/">Illinois</a><span>→</span><strong>Winnebago County</strong>
  </nav>

  <header class="article_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL SURVEILLANCE · WINNEBAGO COUNTY, ILLINOIS</p>
    <h1>Winnebago County</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">County-level findings are kept separate from municipal systems. Drill into a city or village for municipal findings; an unresearched municipality is an open research file, not a claim that surveillance is absent.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">MUNICIPALITIES · OFFICIAL BOUNDARIES</p>
    <h2>Drill down from Winnebago County to the municipality.</h2>
    <p>The directory is based on the Illinois State Archives local-government index and cross-checked against Winnebago County's own jurisdiction directory. Municipal polygons are loaded from Illinois government GIS data.</p>

    <div class="map_legend" aria-label="Municipality map legend">
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_covered"></i><strong>Research available</strong></span>
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_open"></i><strong>Unresearched</strong></span>
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_cross_county"></i><strong>Crosses county line</strong></span>
    </div>

    <CountyMunicipalityMap county="Winnebago" municipalities={winnebagoMunicipalities} />

    <div class="jurisdiction_cards municipality_directory">
      {winnebagoMunicipalities.map(municipality => (
        <a href={`/illinois/counties/winnebago/cities/${municipality.slug}/`}>
          <strong>{municipality.name}</strong>
          <span>{municipality.form.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + municipality.form.slice(1)} · {municipality.status === 'documented' ? 'Municipal dossier available' : 'Research needed'}{municipality.crossCounty ? ` · also in ${municipality.counties.filter(c => c !== 'Winnebago').join(', ')} County` : ''}</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="map_note">
      <a href={winnebagoMunicipalitySources.stateArchives}>Illinois State Archives local-government index</a> ·
      <a href={winnebagoMunicipalitySources.countyDirectory}>Winnebago County jurisdiction directory</a> ·
      <a href={winnebagoMunicipalitySources.censusPlaces}>Census incorporated-place index</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">WINNEBAGO COUNTY SHERIFF'S OFFICE</p>
    <h2>Countywide Flock deployment and drones.</h2>
    <div class="finding_grid">
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Five-year Flock agreement</h3>
        <p>Winnebago County approved a five-year agreement with Flock Group in May 2024 for license-plate readers deployed throughout the county. The appropriation was $719,250, with $174,250 for the first year and $136,250 for each subsequent year.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Federal-seizure funding</h3>
        <p>The county's executive summary identifies the Federal Seizure account as the funding source for the initial unbudgeted appropriation.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Nine drones / 13 reported flights</h3>
        <p>Illinois' SFY 2024 drone report lists the Sheriff's Department as owning nine drones and reports 13 flights in the reporting data.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">FOLLOW-UP NEEDED</span>
        <h3>Current reader count and sharing remain unresolved</h3>
        <p>NoRec has not yet published primary records establishing the Sheriff's Office's complete current ALPR inventory, exact deployment locations, sharing configuration, authorized-user count, or audit results.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PublicRecords records={winnebagoCountyRecords} />

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">UNRESOLVED</p>
    <h2>Records still worth obtaining.</h2>
    <ul class="about_questions">
      <li>Current Winnebago County ALPR inventory and device locations.</li>
      <li>Flock retention, sharing, hotlist, and authorized-user configuration.</li>
      <li>Search and audit logs or annual audit results.</li>
      <li>Current Sheriff drone inventory, payloads, policies, and flight logs.</li>
      <li>Inter-agency agreements governing countywide search or camera access.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
